 On Paseo 0.11.0 or a later release, install the reviewed version from the plugin directory:
 
@@ -163,6 +163,14 @@ The button switches the chat through the same checks as **Apply** and `/account`
 
 To skip the click, set **When a limit runs out during a chat** to **Switch automatically** under a provider in Accounts. The control appears for a provider with more than one account, and the default is **Offer a switch**. The chat rotates through every signed-in account with room, choosing the largest remaining room first, and continues by itself. When all accounts are exhausted, it waits for the next known reset, refreshes the limits, and resumes on the account that becomes usable. After a completed Claude turn the plugin switches but does not send **Continue.**, because the turn may really have finished; the row reads *Switched automatically from Work to Second. Your next message runs on Second.* Like the other chat lines, these rows live in the daemon's memory and are best effort.
 
+### Existing Codex providers and remote accounts
+
+Custom providers such as `codex-work` can opt into a configured Codex pool. A quota-failed task keeps its Paseo tab, native thread, model, workspace, and permissions while its next process uses another eligible account. The chat records the active account; the provider label remains the tab's original provider.
+
+Pool membership lives in Paseo configuration. Candidates need a paid ChatGPT plan, verified native quota, and the exact model. Unavailable readings do not count as capacity. If no candidate qualifies, recovery waits and checks again; adding an eligible account can release that wait. A native quota failure triggers recovery; ordinary network errors, successful turns, and canceled turns do not.
+
+See [configured Codex pools](docs/installation.md#configured-codex-pools) for configuration, removal, and the remote-history trust boundary. This pool is separate from managed-account sign-in and manual `/account` selection.
+
 ## Read limits
 
 Each account shows all reported limit windows, including zero usage. Measured windows show used and remaining percentages and a reset countdown. Codex usage-based workspace plans show their monthly credit allowance as a limit, with the credits left; Claude enterprise seats show their monthly spend allowance the same way. Expand details for exact local reset times, durations, fetch/check timestamps, and windows without data.
